findings.expected:
Workspace AGENTS.md, 'Self-tests and tests come with every coin and feature':
- every feature has a quick startup known answer (line 65);
- 'a known answer compares exact output, and a verifier is also given a case it must refuse' (line 66);
- only slower checks, such as scrypt or full-size Argon2, go to the full self-test (line 67).

Strength::of takes about a millisecond, so slowness does not justify keeping its only check at the full tier. The specification leaves strength policy to the application (mhfe_spec/README.md:316), so this rests on the AGENTS.md rule, not on the specification.

Workspace AGENTS.md rule 6 (lines 47-51):
- 'Every rule, check, validation, limit, constant, conversion, message, list of answers and data shape has exactly one source';
- 'the same question, list of answers or message is built in one place';
- 'Two blocks that differ only in a value become one function with a parameter';
- an allowed copy says why in a comment, with a test that keeps the copies in step.

None of these copies has such a comment.

